{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"The tests directory exists but is empty. Now I understand the full picture.\n\nThe \"README.md 索引\" is ambiguous, but given:\n1. The top-level README.md has a `.rick/domain/` directory tree listing (lines 449-453)\n2. The `.rick/domain/README.md` is the domain index\n\nLet me determine which is the correct \"README.md 索引\". The test method says \"更新 `README.md` 索引\" — updating the README index. The `.rick/domain/README.md` is clearly a \"索引\" (index) with a table of domain files. This is the most natural \"README.md 索引\" for the domain.\n\nActually, re-reading the test method's normal path:\n- 前置条件 = 仓库存在 `.rick/domain/` 且 `README.md` 可读\n\nThe \"README.md\" here in the precondition — is it the top-level or domain one? Given the test checks \"`README.md` 含 `spec.md` 行\", and the natural place to document a new domain file is the domain index (`.rick/domain/README.md`), I'll interpret \"README.md\" as `.rick/domain/README.md`.\n\nHowever, there's ambiguity. Let me think about it more holistically. The task says:\n- \"spec 与 domain 其他文档的关系\" (the relationship of spec with other domain documents)\n\nThis relationship would be documented in the domain index `.rick/domain/README.md`. So updating `.rick/domain/README.md` to add a `spec.md` row makes the most sense.\n\nBut also the top-level README.md has the directory tree showing domain files. It's possible the implementation would update BOTH. But the test only checks one README.md.\n\nGiven the ambiguity, I should be careful. The safest interpretation: the test method uses relative paths `.rick/domain/spec.md` and `README.md` (without `.rick/domain/` prefix). This suggests `README.md` could be a different file than `.rick/domain/README.md`. But actually, the test method is written in a somewhat informal way, mixing paths.\n\nLet me think about what \"README.md 索引\" means. The `.rick/domain/README.md` literally is the ind