{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"Now I understand the full task structure. Task1 is about defining the spec standard and acceptance criteria. Task2 will produce the actual spec.md (rick's first spec). \n\nWait, but the test method for task1 says \"写 `.rick/domain/spec.md`\". Let me re-read the task1 goal:\n\n\"Task Goal: 升级 rick 项目的 domain 描述方法，新增「spec」概念（KR1.1 + KR1.3）。spec = 结构化自然语言描述的工程实现契约。产出 spec 规范文档：定义 spec 的结构模板（四要素：模块边界 / 职责 / 接口契约 / 验收标准）、spec 与 domain 其他文档的关系，以及 spec 的验收标准定义...\"\n\nSo task1 produces a \"spec 规范文档\" (spec specification document) that defines the spec template and acceptance criteria. This document should be written to `.rick/domain/spec.md`.\n\nActually wait, let me reconsider. Task1 = KR1.1 (define spec standard) + KR1.3 (define spec acceptance criteria). The output is \"spec 规范文档\" — a document defining the spec structure template.\n\nTask2 = KR1.2 (produce rick's first spec). Task2 will \"产出 rick 第一份 spec（四层架构 + 5 模块 + env 四职责契约）\".\n\nSo task1's spec.md is the \"spec 规范文档\" (the meta-spec: what a spec looks like), while task2 produces the actual spec content for rick.\n\nHmm, but both would be `.rick/domain/spec.md`? That would conflict. Let me think.\n\nActually, task1 defines the spec规范 (the template/structure), which is written as a document. This document `.rick/domain/spec.md` describes:\n- The four-element structure template (模块边界 / 职责 / 接口契约 / 验收标准)\n- The relationship between spec and other domain documents\n- The acceptance criteria definition (spec → 开发计划 → 功能等价实现)\n\nTask2 then produces rick's first actual spec (the content filled in with the four-layer architecture + 5 modules + env four responsibilities).\n\nWait, but where would task2's spec go? It would also be `.rick/domain/spec.md`? Or a different file?\n\nActually, looking more carefully, the test method for task1 is testing `.rick/domain/spec.md`. The test checks:\n1. `.rick/domain/spec.md` exists\n2. README.md index contains `spec.md` line\n3. Four keywords: 模块边界, 职责, 接口契约, 验收标准\n4. `功能等价` ≥ 1\n5. `{{` = 0 (no template variable leakage)\n6. `dry-run|go test|集成测试` enumerated (actionable criteria)\n\nSo task1's spec.md is the spec规范文档 that describes the template AND the acceptance criteria. It should contain:\n- The four-element template sections (模块边界/职责/接口契约/验收标准) — as the template definition\n- `功能等价` — as the acceptance criteria\n- No `{{` (no leftover template placeholders)\n- Enumerated actionable criteria (`dry-run`, `go test`, `集成测试`)\n\nThis makes sense. The spec.md is the \"spec规范\" document, which itself contains the four-element structure and the acceptance criteria (功能等价 = 通过所有功能验收, with examples of actionable acceptance criteria like dry-run/go test/集成测试).\n\nSo my test script should verify all these in `.rick/domain/spec.md`.\n\nNow about the README.md index: which README.md? The task1 goal says \"spec 与 domain 其他文档的关系\" — this relationship is documented. The domain index is `.rick/domain/README.md`. I'll check that `.rick/domain/README.md` contains a `spec.md` line.\n\nActually, let me reconsider once more. The test method says:\n- 前置条件 = 仓库存在 `.rick/domain/` 且 `README.md` 可读\n\n\"仓库存在 `.rick/domain/` 且 `README.md` 可读\" — the repo has `.rick/domain/` and README.md is readable. This phrasing \"仓库...且 README.md 可读\" — the README.md is at repo root? Or in domain?\n\nGiven the path convention in the test method, `.rick/domain/spec.md` uses the full relative path. If they meant `.rick/domain/README.md`, they'd probably write `.rick/domain/README.md`. They wrote \"README.md\" which in the context of \"更新 README.md 索引\" and \"README.md 含 spec.md 行\".\n\nHmm. Let me think about which is more semantically correct for the domain index.\n\nActually, I found it. The `.rick/domain/README.md` contains a table \"| 文件 | 内容 |\" with rows like \"| `architecture.md` | ... |\". This is the domain index. When you add a new domain file (spec.md), you add a row \"| `spec.md` | ... |\" to this table.\n\nThe top-level README.md contains the `.rick/` directory tree listing domain files. This is also a kind of index, but less direct.\n\nBoth are plausible. But the phrase \"README.md 索引\" strongly implies \"the README that serves as an index\", which for domain files is `.rick/domain/README.md`.\n\nActually, I realize I should consider: the task1 goal explicitly lists \"spec 与 domain 其他文档的关系\" as part of what the spec规范文档 should define. This is about the spec's relationship to OTHER domain documents (architecture.md, commands.md, etc.). This relationship is naturally documented in the domain index `.rick/domain/README.md`.\n\nI'll go with `.rick/domain/README.md` as the \"README.md 索引\". But wait — let me reconsider if it could be the top-level README.md.\n\nThe test method normal path expectation: \"`README.md` 含 `spec.md` 行\". If I check the top-level README.md, it currently doesn't have spec.md in its tree (it lists architecture.md, commands.md, go-patterns.md, testing-conventions.md, project-conventions.md). So after the task, the top-level README.md's directory tree should be updated to include spec.md too.\n\nHmm, but this is task1, and task12 is \"README/wiki 文档同步\". So maybe the top-level README sync is done in task12, not task1.\n\nActually, task1 is about the spec规范文档 itself. The \"README.md 索引\" most likely refers to `.rick/domain/README.md`.\n\nI need to make a decision. Let me go with a robust approach: check `.rick/domain/README.md` (the domain index) for the `spec.md` line, since that's the natural \"README.md 索引\" for domain files, AND it's the most direct interpretation of \"更新 README.md 索引\".\n\nActually, wait. Let me reconsider the whole thing from the test method's perspective, being very literal:\n\n\"预期 = `test -f .rick/domain/spec.md` 返回 0，`README.md` 含 `spec.md` 行\"\n\nTwo assertions:\n1. `.rick/domain/spec.md` exists\n2. `README.md` contains `spec.md` line\n\nSince assertion 1 uses `.rick/domain/spec.md` (full path), and assertion 2 uses just `README.md` (no path), these could refer to different base directories. But both are relative to the repo root presumably.\n\nIf README.md = `.rick/domain/README.md`, then assertion 2 checks the domain index.\n\nI think the most defensible reading, given the task is \"升级 domain 描述方法\" and the domain index is `.rick/domain/README.md`, is:\n\n- README.md 索引 = `.rick/domain/README.md`\n\nLet me go with checking `.rick/domain/README.md`. I'll make this clear in the test with comments.\n\nActually, you know what, let me reconsider even more holistically. There's a subtle issue: the task says \"写 `.rick/domain/spec.md` + 更新 `README.md` 索引\". The \"README.md 索引\" — in Chinese, this means \"README.md index\". The `.rick/domain/README.md` is literally the index of the domain directory. So \"更新 README.md 索引\" = \"update the domain README index\" = update `.rick/domain/README.md`.\n\nFinal decision: check `.rick/domain/README.md` contains `spec.md`.\n\nBut hold on, to be safe and avoid false negatives (test passing when it should fail) OR false positives (test failing when feature is actually correct), let me think about what could go wrong:\n\n- If I check `.rick/domain/README.md` and the implementer updates the top-level README.md instead, the test would fail even though the \"spirit\" is met. But that's actually a legitimate test failure per the acceptance criteria (they should update the domain index).\n\n- If I check the top-level README.md and the implementer updates `.rick/domain/README.md`, the test fails.\n\nThe test method is the spec here. I should follow it as literally as reasonable. The most literal reading of \"README.md 索引\" combined with \"spec 与 domain 其他文档的关系\" is `.rick/domain/README.md`.\n\nLet me make the final decision and also consider: should I check BOTH? No — the test method specifies \"README.md 含 spec.md 行\" as a single assertion. I'll check `.rick/domain/README.md`.\n\nActually, let me reconsider one more time whe