ck/domain/spec.md`.\n\nActually wait, let me reconsider. Task1 = KR1.1 (define spec standard) + KR1.3 (define spec acceptance criteria). The output is \"spec 规范文档\" — a document defining the spec structure template.\n\nTask2 = KR1.2 (produce rick's first spec). Task2 will \"产出 rick 第一份 spec（四层架构 + 5 模块 + env 四职责契约）\".\n\nSo task1's spec.md is the \"spec 规范文档\" (the meta-spec: what a spec looks like), while task2 produces the actual spec content for rick.\n\nHmm, but both would be `.rick/domain/spec.md`? That would conflict. Let me think.\n\nActually, task1 defines the spec规范 (the template/structure), which is written as a document. This document `.rick/domain/spec.md` describes:\n- The four-element structure template (模块边界 / 职责 / 接口契约 / 验收标准)\n- The relationship between spec and other domain documents\n- The acceptance criteria definition (spec → 开发计划 → 功能等价实现)\n\nTask2 then produces rick's first actual spec (the content filled in with the four-layer architecture + 5 modules + env four responsibilities).\n\nWait, but where would task2's spec go? It would also be `.rick/domain/spec.md`? Or a different file?\n\nActually, looking more carefully, the test method for task1 is testing `.rick/domain/spec.md`. The test checks:\n1. `.rick/domain/spec.md` exists\n2. README.md index contains `spec.md` line\n3. Four keywords: 模块边界, 职责, 接口契约, 验收标准\n4. `功能等价` ≥ 1\n5. `{{` = 0 (no template variable leakage)\n6. `dry-run|go test|集成测试` enumerated (actionable criteria)\n\nSo task1's spec.md is the spec规范文档 that describes the template AND the acceptance criteria. It should contain:\n- The four-element template sections (模块边界/职责/接口契约/验收标准) — as the template definition\n- `功能等价` — as the acceptance criteria\n- No `{{` (no leftover template placeholders)\n- Enumerated actionable criteria (`dry-run`, `go test`, `集成测试`)\n\nThis makes sense. The spec.md is the \"spec规范\" document, which itself contains the four-element structure and the acceptance criteria (功能等价 = 通过所有功能验收, with examples of