"README.md index\". The `.rick/domain/README.md` is literally the index of the domain directory. So \"更新 README.md 索引\" = \"update the domain README index\" = update `.rick/domain/README.md`.\n\nFinal decision: check `.rick/domain/README.md` contains `spec.md`.\n\nBut hold on, to be safe and avoid false negatives (test passing when it should fail) OR false positives (test failing when feature is actually correct), let me think about what could go wrong:\n\n- If I check `.rick/domain/README.md` and the implementer updates the top-level README.md instead, the test would fail even though the \"spirit\" is met. But that's actually a legitimate test failure per the acceptance criteria (they should update the domain index).\n\n- If I check the top-level README.md and the implementer updates `.rick/domain/README.md`, the test fails.\n\nThe test method is the spec here. I should follow it as literally as reasonable. The most literal reading of \"README.md 索引\" combined with \"spec 与 domain 其他文档的关系\" is `.rick/domain/README.md`.\n\nLet me make the final decision and also consider: should I check BOTH? No — the test method specifies \"README.md 含 spec.md 行\" as a single assertion. I'll check `.rick/domain/README.md`.\n\nActually, let me reconsider one more time whether there might be additional context. Let me check if there are other tasks' test prompts or any hints about which README. Let me check the prompts directory.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_9IZxjHnx9JQ3jpuBXbZk7800","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick && ls -la .rick/jobs/job_35/doing/prompts/ && echo \"=== tasks dir ===\" && ls -la .rick/jobs/job_35/doing/tasks/"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":1678,"output":2208,"cacheRead":27008,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":2107,"totalTokens":30894,"cost":{"input":0.00072993,"output":0.00192096,"cacheRead":0.000097904,"cacheWrite":0,"to